lfcr|Encoding & conversion|Converts line endings.|autolf on this disk does the job.|TOP release 2 (The OS-9 Project, Munich), top.tar.Z
linkup|Needs hardware|LinkUp, a K-Windows communications suite with ansishow, audioplay, gport and terminal.|The clients need a K-Windows display, and its installer writes over the root disk.|Microware OS-9 archive, KWIN_LinkUp_1_0.lzh
link|Files & directories|Makes a hard link by writing a directory entry to the raw disk.|RBF has no hard links; a program that made one this way corrupted this disk. Its author warns to use it at your own risk.|comp.os.os9, January 1989
ln|Files & directories|Makes a hard link by writing a directory entry to the raw disk.|RBF has no hard links; a program that made one this way corrupted this disk. Its author warns to use it at your own risk.|comp.os.os9, January 1989
loglist|System & modules|A 1988 utility that lists the system's log file.|No source, no documentation and no terms anywhere.|EFFO public-domain disk 1
lpunch|Encoding & conversion|Converts punched-card deck records.|There is nothing here to use them with.|Microware OS-9 archive, 6809 C section
malawi|Games|A two-player board game.|It is written for X11 only.|comp.sources.games v17i074
marquis|Screen toys|Scrolls a message along a terminal's status line from the background.|No terminal in the disk's termcap has a status line, and it will not start without one.|comp.sources.misc v07i089
mb (banner)|Text tools|Prints large banners from an external font.|The author ships no font, so it would arrive unable to print anything.|comp.sources.unix v26i141, banners collection
mb|Amusements|A text filter from the silly collection.|Left out on content.|alt.sources, December 1992, silly.tar
